{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Chatbot.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Chatbot.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"chatbot chatbot","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Chatbot.md","fileName":"Chatbot.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Chatbot","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Virtual Assistant Architecture]] [[Microsoft Bot Framework Applications]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Virtual Assistant Architecture","Microsoft Bot Framework Applications","Intent Classification","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aiassistants.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Chatbot.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Chatbot.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"chatbot chatbot","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Chatbot.md","fileName":"Chatbot.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Chatbot","heading":"Chatbot","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A chatbot is a conversational program whose primary interface is typed or spoken dialogue. Some chatbots are open-ended social systems, while others are narrow agents that answer questions or complete transactions.\n\nThe category describes the interaction form, not a guaranteed level of intelligence. A chatbot may rely on scripted rules, statistical [[Intent Classification]], learned generation, or a combination of these methods.\n\nThe Bot Framework project describes a chatbot as a conversational state machine whose framework manages service and channel plumbing. Message activities enter through the bot adapter, language understanding selects an intent, and the bot chooses and sends an appropriate reply.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Virtual Assistant Architecture","Microsoft Bot Framework Applications","Intent Classification","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aiassistants.epub